# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
#
# Standalone unbounded proof for rtl/lca_modmul_fast.sv.
#
# Run with the repository's pinned Yosys:
#
#   node --experimental-wasm-exnref tools/run_yosys.mjs \
#       -s formal/lca_modmul_fast_formal.ys
#
# This script is deliberately NOT wired into `make formal`: the fast
# multiplier is not part of the E1 evidence chain yet (see
# docs/FAST_REDUCTION.md). formal/prove.ys is left byte-identical.
#
# What is proven, by temporal induction with every input unconstrained on
# every cycle and the base case starting from the zero (reset) state, so the
# properties hold at all times rather than up to a bound:
#
#   P1  req_ready is exactly the pipeline-advance condition;
#   P2  an unaccepted response holds valid with an identical fault flag and
#       product for as long as reset stays deasserted;
#   P3  back-pressure freezes every pipeline register, so no in-flight
#       request is dropped, reordered or corrupted by a stall;
#   P4  a faulting response carries a zero product - fail closed;
#   A1  the ML-KEM stage-B result is canonical for q=3329 over the whole
#       2**24 product domain;
#   A2  the ML-KEM stage-C result is canonical for q=3329 over every 12-bit
#       stage-2 payload;
#   A3  the ML-DSA stage-C result is canonical for q=8380417 over every one
#       of the 2**48 possible stage-2 payloads, i.e. the four-fold Solinas
#       bound chain is proven at full width;
#   A4  the registered response product is canonical for the modulus that
#       produced it.
#
# A1-A4 are range proofs. Congruence to (a*b) mod q is NOT proven here; that
# is simulation and model evidence (exhaustive for q=3329 in
# tests/test_fastmod.py, randomized plus boundary for q=8380417).

design -reset
read_verilog -formal -sv rtl/lca_modmul_fast.sv
prep -top lca_modmul_fast
flatten
chformal -lower
sat -tempinduct -verify -prove-asserts -set-assumes -set-init-zero -maxsteps 30
